Date: 2026-10-17

diff --git a/references/trace-recording.md b/references/trace-recording.md
index fcfdd1d..6d83e04 100644
--- a/references/trace-recording.md
+++ b/references/trace-recording.md
@@ -59,15 +59,19 @@ recording to end cleanly:
 ```bash
 # Start recording (background)
 python3 "${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/record_trace.py" \
-  --attach Helm --stop-file /tmp/stop-trace \
+  --attach Helm --stop-file "$PWD/tmp/stop-trace" \
   --output ~/Desktop/session.trace
 
 # ...user does their thing...
 
 # Stop cleanly (from another shell or tool call)
-touch /tmp/stop-trace
+touch "$PWD/tmp/stop-trace"
 ```
 
+Keep the stop-file in the project's own `tmp/` folder, never the shared
+system `/tmp`, where a leftover or planted file would end the next
+recording as soon as it starts.
+
 The script polls every 0.5s for the stop-file, sends SIGINT to xctrace
 when it appears, and waits up to 60s for the trace to finalise.
 
@@ -136,7 +140,7 @@ path straight into `analyze_trace.py`:
 
 ```bash
 TRACE=$(python3 "${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/record_trace.py" \
-    --attach Helm --stop-file /tmp/stop-trace --output ~/Desktop/session.trace \
+    --attach Helm --stop-file "$PWD/tmp/stop-trace" --output ~/Desktop/session.trace \
     2>&1 | awk '/trace written:/ {print $NF}')
 python3 "${SKILL_DIR}/scripts/analyze_trace.py" --trace "$TRACE" --json-only
 ```
